Hello, Thanks for contacting EA.

In your recent email, you did not include enough information for us to
effectively troubleshoot your situation.In order to help you to solve
the
problem you're experiencing we will need more info about your system
and
the
methods you are employing to run the game.

If you need further assistance, please include the following
information
in
the text of your email message:

1) The name of the game you are having difficulty with.

2) If the game is a dual executable, please specify whether you are
running
the Windows95 version with DirectX or the MSDOS version.

3) Please include the following system info:
a) Processor type and speed (i.e. Intel Pentium 166mhz)
b) The make and model of your video card (i.e. ATI Mach32 PCI 2mb)
c) The make and model of your sound card (i.e. Creative Labs
SoundBlaster 16
Plug-and-Play)
d) The amount of RAM memory installed on the system. (i.e. 16
megabytes)

IF YOU DO NOT KNOW ANY OF THE ABOVE INFORMATION, PLEASE CONSULT YOUR
SYSTEM
SUMMARY PROVIDED BY YOUR SYSTEM VENDOR. ALTERNATELY, THIS INFO CAN
USUALLY BE
DETERMINED BY FOLLOWING THE PROCEDURE BELOW USING WINDOWS 95:
a) Click the Start Button. Select SETTINGS and then CONTROL PANEL.
From
the
control panel window, find SYSTEM and double left click the icon. It
will
bring up a window titled SYSTEM PROPERTIES. The Processor Type and
amount of
RAM memory are listed under COMPUTER. Clicking the DEVICE MANAGER tab
at
the
top of the window will bring up the DEVICE MANAGER section. Your Video
information can be found under DISPLAY ADAPTERS. Your Sound Card info
is
under SOUND, VIDEO and GAME CONTROLLERS.

4) A listing of the contents of your AUTOEXEC.BAT and CONFIG.SYS files
found
at the root of your C:\ directory. Please include this as part of the
TEXT of
your email message. (NOT as an attachment)

The more information you give, the more able we are to help you.

Thanks,
